# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 292-296 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, RUN 3, 2026-09-26): THE WRESTLERS — no peace out of struggle
# (Abram and Lot again), the parties, no slaves, the court's agent's wife, intent for shame, the life-threatening grip (292); "cut off her hand" — the rescue by
# her hand or her life, and R. Judah's money by 19:21 (293); THE WEIGHTS — a stone and a stone, the sela's wear, keeping is having, the ephah, the four-kav
# measure, the local custom for weighing and heaping, the market inspector and the thirty days, the ephah's two sizes (294); the reward beside it, even one of
# these, no mixing, the five names (295 — HEADLESS inside 25:15); AMALEK — mouth and heart, the way and the exodus, the chance, the stragglers, measure for
# measure, the rest, the conquest, the two blottings (296). Every row READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_. Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(292, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN MEN STRUGGLE TOGETHER" (25:11) — NO PEACE COMES OUT OF STRUGGLE; GENESIS 13:7 AGAIN — WHAT MADE LOT PART FROM THAT RIGHTEOUS ONE? STRIFE; "WHEN THERE IS A QUARREL" (25:1) — WHAT MADE THIS ONE BE FLOGGED? STRIFE. The head row of piska 292 — READ BEFORE at Genesis 29\'s ledger, REREAD WHOLE here ({SP_(292, 1, "אין", "שלום", "יוצא", "מתוך", "נצות")} "no peace comes out of struggle"; {SP_(292, 1, "מי", "גרם", "ללוט", "שיפרוש", "מאותו", "צדיק")} "what caused Lot to part from that righteous one?"; {SP_(292, 1, "הוי", "אומר", "זו", "מריבה")} "say: it is strife"): 286:1\'s homily repeated for the chapter\'s second quarrel verse — Abram and Lot the prototype of both. Reread.')
srow(292, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"MEN" — ONLY MEN? A MAN WITH A WOMAN, A WOMAN WITH A MAN — WHENCE? "TOGETHER" — ANYONE. ({SP_(292, 2, "איש", "עם", "אשה", "אשה", "עם", "איש", "מנין")} "a man with a woman, a woman with a man — whence?"; {SP_(292, 2, "יחדו", "מכל", "מקום")} "\'together\' — anyone"): 286:2\'s widening for the wrestlers. Fresh.')
srow(292, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"A MAN AND HIS BROTHER" — EXCLUDING SLAVES, WHO HAVE NO BROTHERHOOD. ({SP_(292, 3, "פרט", "לעבדים", "שאין", "להם", "אחוה")} "excluding slaves, who have no brotherhood"): the parties free men — the slave outside the shame payment (the Tosefta\'s row the English names); one of the chapter\'s rows citing no verse in the Hebrew. Fresh.')
srow(292, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE WIFE OF THE ONE DRAWS NEAR" — NOT THE WIFE OF THE COURT\'S AGENT; "TO SAVE HER HUSBAND" — RABBI: SINCE THE TORAH HAS DAMAGES WHERE THE UNINTENDING IS AS THE INTENDING, HERE TOO? "AND SEIZES HIS SECRETS" — NOT LIABLE FOR THE SHAME UNTIL HE INTENDS. ({SP_(292, 4, "ולא", "אשת", "שליח", "בית", "דין")} "and not the wife of the court\'s agent"; {SP_(292, 4, "שאין", "מתכוין", "כמתכוין")} "the unintending as the intending"; {SP_(292, 4, "שאינו", "חיב", "על", "הבשת", "עד", "שיתכוין")} "not liable for the shame until he intends"): THE INTENT PARAMETER of the shame payment (Bava Kamma 8:3\'s row, the English\'s "//"; the design\'s DV25-04 with Bava Kamma 8:1) — the parser\'s [1] "the one" (starred) read as whose wife; the court\'s agent beaten with no claim. Fresh.')
srow(292, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"HIS SECRETS" — ONLY THESE? ANYTHING WITH DANGER IN IT WHENCE? "AND SEIZES" — ANY; WHY "HIS SECRETS"? AS THEY HOLD DANGER TO LIFE AND STAND UNDER "CUT OFF HER HAND", SO ANYTHING WITH DANGER TO LIFE. ({SP_(292, 5, "לרבות", "דבר", "שיש", "בו", "סכנה")} "to include anything with danger in it"; {SP_(292, 5, "שיש", "בו", "סכנת", "נפשות")} "with danger to life in it"): the class by prototype — the life-threatening grip, 293:1\'s rescue its consequence. Fresh.')
srow(293, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL CUT OFF HER HAND" (25:12) — YOU ARE BOUND TO SAVE HIM BY HER HAND; IF YOU CANNOT SAVE HIM BY HER HAND, SAVE HIM BY HER LIFE — "YOUR EYE SHALL NOT PITY". The head row of piska 293 ({SP_(293, 1, "שאתה", "חיב", "להצילה", "בכפה")} "you are bound to save by her hand"; {SP_(293, 1, "הצילה", "בנפשה")} "save by her life"): THE PURSUER\'S LAW read into the verse (243:2\'s kin at the betrothed girl) — the rescuer stops the attacker by a limb, else by her life; the first of the verse\'s two readings. Fresh.')
srow(293, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH: "YOUR EYE SHALL NOT PITY" SAID HERE AND THERE (19:21): AS THERE IT IS MONEY, SO HERE IT IS MONEY. READ BEFORE at chapters 19-21\'s ledger (the plotting witnesses\' "eye for eye"), REREAD WHOLE here ({SP_(293, 2, "האמור", "להלן", "ממון")} "said there — money"; {SP_(293, 2, "האמור", "כאן", "ממון")} "said here — money"): THE PITY FORMULA\'S OPERATOR — "cut off her hand" IS THE HAND\'S VALUE IN MONEY by the verbal analogy to 19:21 (16b\'s operator; the design\'s DV25-04); the verse\'s second reading — the compile takes the payment, 293:1 the rescue. Reread.')
srow(294, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT HAVE IN YOUR BAG A STONE AND A STONE" (25:13) — NO LITRA, HALF LITRA AND QUARTER LITRA? "GREAT AND SMALL" — A GREAT ONE THAT BELIES THE SMALL, TAKING WITH THE GREAT AND RETURNING WITH THE SMALL. The head row of piska 294 ({SP_(294, 1, "ליטרא", "וחצי", "ליטרא", "ורביע", "ליטרא")} "a litra, a half litra and a quarter litra"; {SP_(294, 1, "גדולה", "שהיא", "מכחשת", "את", "הקטנה")} "a great one that belies the small"; {SP_(294, 1, "נוטל", "בגדולה", "ומחזיר", "בקטנה")} "takes with the great and returns with the small"): the bar not on a set of weights but on two of one name — "a stone and a stone" Proverbs 20:10\'s phrase (find 16); the design\'s DV25-04 with Bava Batra 5:10-11. Fresh.')
srow(294, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA: WHENCE THAT ONE MAKES NO SELA LESS THAN A SHEKEL, NO DINAR LESS THAN A HALF-DINAR? "YOU SHALL NOT HAVE". ({SP_(294, 2, "סלע", "פחות", "משקל")} "a sela less than a shekel"; {SP_(294, 2, "ולא", "דינר", "פחות", "מטרפעיקא")} "nor a dinar less than a tarpe\'ik (a half-dinar)"): THE COIN\'S WEAR — a worn coin a false weight; the tolerable loss the Tosefta\'s parameter (the English\'s Bava Metzia rows). Fresh.')
srow(294, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE B. R. JUDAH: IF YOU KEPT IT, IT IS UNDER "YOU SHALL NOT HAVE". ({SP_(294, 3, "אם", "קימת")} "if you kept it"; {SP_(294, 3, "הרי", "הוא", "בלא", "יהיה", "לך")} "it is under \'you shall not have\'"): possession the offense without use — the verb "have" the whole law; the second row of the chapter citing nothing (the ink). Fresh.')
srow(294, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT HAVE IN YOUR HOUSE AN EPHAH AND AN EPHAH" (25:14) — NO TARKAV, HALF AND QUARTER? "GREAT AND SMALL" — THE GREAT THAT BELIES THE SMALL. ({SP_(294, 4, "תרקב", "וחצי", "תרקב", "ורביע", "תרקב")} "a tarkav (two kav), a half and a quarter"; {SP_(294, 4, "גדולה", "שהיא", "מכחשת", "את", "הקטנה")} "a great one that belies the small"): 294:1\'s form for the dry measure; 25:14 carries no head. Fresh.')
srow(294, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER: WHENCE THAT A MAN MAKES NO FOUR-KAV MEASURE TO MEASURE WITH IN HIS HOUSE? "YOU SHALL NOT HAVE". ({SP_(294, 5, "מדה", "בת", "ארבעת", "קבים")} "a measure of four kav"; {SP_(294, 5, "מודד", "בה", "בתוך", "ביתו")} "measuring with it in his house"): a non-standard size barred even at home. Fresh.')
srow(294, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT ONE WEIGHS NOT EXACTLY WHERE THEY TIP THE SCALE, NOR TIPS WHERE THEY WEIGH EXACTLY? "A WHOLE STONE" (25:15); EVEN IF HE SAID "I WEIGH EXACTLY WHERE THEY TIP, TO LOWER THE PRICE"? "AND JUST SHALL YOU HAVE". ({SP_(294, 6, "שאין", "מעינים", "במקום", "שמכריעים")} "one does not weigh exactly where they tip the scale"; {SP_(294, 6, "לפחות", "לו", "מן", "הדמים")} "to lower the price for him"; {SP_(294, 6, "וצדק", "יהיה", "לך")} "and just shall you have"): THE LOCAL CUSTOM the parameter — the market\'s way binds even with the buyer\'s consent and to his gain (Bava Batra 5:11\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(294, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT ONE HEAPS NOT WHERE THEY LEVEL, NOR LEVELS WHERE THEY HEAP? "A WHOLE STONE"; EVEN "I LEVEL WHERE THEY HEAP, TO LOWER THE PRICE" — THEY DO NOT LISTEN TO HIM? "AND JUST SHALL YOU HAVE". ({SP_(294, 7, "שלא", "יגדוש", "במקום", "שמוחקים")} "that one heap not where they level"; {SP_(294, 7, "ולא", "ימחוק", "במקום", "שגודשים")} "nor level where they heap"; {SP_(294, 7, "שאין", "שומעים", "לו")} "they do not listen to him"): 294:6\'s rule for the dry measure — heaped or level by the place (Bava Batra 5:11). Fresh.')
srow(294, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"SHALL YOU HAVE" — APPOINT A MARKET INSPECTOR FOR IT; HENCE: THE WHOLESALER WIPES HIS MEASURES ONCE IN THIRTY DAYS, THE HOUSEHOLDER ONCE IN TWELVE MONTHS — ETC., THE MISHNAH. ({SP_(294, 8, "מנה", "אגרונומוס", "על", "כך")} "appoint a market inspector (agronomos) for it"; {SP_(294, 8, "הסיטון", "מקנח", "מדותיו", "אחת", "לשלשים", "יום")} "the wholesaler wipes his measures once in thirty days"; {SP_(294, 8, "אחת", "לשנים", "עשר", "חדש")} "once in twelve months"): Bava Batra 5:10 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=", its rest supplied in braces) — THE MISHNAH BY ABBREVIATION (the sitting\'s sixth), THE GREEK LOANWORD agronomos (the market officer; kruspedin the tassels\' Greek name in RUN 1), and two CLOCKS (thirty days, twelve months) — an office the verse\'s "you shall have" creates. Fresh.')
srow(294, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'ELAZAR B. HANANIAH B. HEZEKIAH B. GARON: EZEKIEL 46:11 "AN EPHAH FOR THE BULL, AN EPHAH FOR THE RAM, AN EPHAH FOR THE LAMB" — IS THEIR MEASURE ONE? NUMBERS 29:3 SAYS THREE TENTHS, TWO, ONE — SO A GREAT EPHAH AND A SMALL EPHAH ARE BOTH CALLED EPHAH. ({SP_(294, 9, "וכי", "מדת", "פרים", "ואילים", "וכבשים", "אחת", "היא")} "is the measure of bulls, rams and lambs one?"; {SP_(294, 9, "שאיפה", "גדולה", "ואיפה", "קטנה", "קרויה", "איפה")} "a great ephah and a small ephah are both called ephah"): the word\'s two sizes proved from the tape\'s own Numbers 29:3 against Ezekiel\'s temple — the noun a class, not a quantity; the piska\'s last row. Fresh.')
srow(295, 1, 'CONTEXT', f'"THAT YOUR DAYS MAY BE LONG" (25:15) — ONE OF THE TORAH\'S COMMANDMENTS WITH ITS REWARD BESIDE IT; AN A FORTIORI: IF A DRIED FIG, ONE HUNDREDTH OF AN ISSAR, EARNS LENGTH OF DAYS, THE COMMANDMENTS THAT COST THE PURSE ALL THE MORE. The head row of the HEADLESS piska 295 (inside 25:15; four rows) ({SP_(295, 1, "שמתן", "שכרה", "בצדה")} "whose reward is given beside it"; {SP_(295, 1, "גרוגרת", "שאינה", "אלא", "אחד", "ממאה", "באסר")} "a dried fig, only one hundredth of an issar"; {SP_(295, 1, "קל", "וחמר")} "an a fortiori argument"): the reward formula (find 9\'s run with 5:16 and 4:40) — the weights and the nest (22:7) the two laws paid beside their verse; a homily on the least weight. Fresh.')
srow(295, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR AN ABOMINATION OF THE LORD YOUR GOD IS EVERYONE WHO DOES THESE" (25:16) — NOT LIABLE UNTIL HE DOES ALL OF THEM? "EVERYONE WHO DOES THESE" — EVEN ONE. ({SP_(295, 2, "עד", "שיעבר", "על", "כלם")} "until he transgresses all of them"; {SP_(295, 2, "אפלו", "אחת", "מהם")} "even one of them"): the abomination formula\'s seventh Deuteronomy seat (find 5; 22:5\'s run of seven) — "these" any one of the four; 25:16 carries no head. Fresh.')
srow(295, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"EVERYONE WHO DOES WRONG" — HENCE: ONE DOES NOT MIX PRODUCE WITH PRODUCE, EVEN NEW WITH OLD, EVEN A SEAH AT A DINAR WITH A SEAH WORTH A DINAR AND A TRESSIS, TO SELL AT A DINAR. ({SP_(295, 3, "אין", "מערבין", "פרות", "בפרות")} "one does not mix produce with produce"; {SP_(295, 3, "ואפלו", "חדשים", "בישנים")} "even new with old"; {SP_(295, 3, "סאה", "בדינר")} "a seah at a dinar"): Bava Metzia 4:11\'s bar on blending (the English\'s "//") — even to the seller\'s loss; the wrong the deception, not the price. Fresh.')
srow(295, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"EVERYONE WHO DOES WRONG" — CALLED BY FIVE NAMES: CONDEMNED, ABOMINATION, DETESTABLE, HATED, PERVERSE. ({SP_(295, 4, "קרוי", "חמשה", "שמות")} "called by five names"; {SP_(295, 4, "חרם", "תועבה", "משקץ", "שנוי", "עול")} "condemned, abomination, detestable, hated, perverse"): 226:3\'s five epithets again (RUN 1, the garments) — the abomination formula\'s subject named the same at 22:5 and 25:16, the run of seven words the two verses share (find 5); the headless piska\'s last row. Fresh.')
srow(296, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"REMEMBER" (25:17) — WITH THE MOUTH; "FORGET NOT" (25:19) — IN THE HEART; SO EXODUS 15:14 "THE PEOPLES HEARD AND TREMBLED". The head row of piska 296 ({SP_(296, 1, "זכור", "בפה")} "remember — with the mouth"; {SP_(296, 1, "אל", "תשכח", "בלב")} "forget not — in the heart"): THE TWO VERBS TWO ORGANS — the reading aloud and the memory (find 10\'s "you shall not forget", twice in the Torah); the Song\'s verse the tape\'s own line before Amalek\'s attack (Exodus 15:14, 17:8) — the design\'s DV25-05. Fresh.')
srow(296, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"ON THE WAY" — IN THE HOUR OF YOUR CONFUSION. ({SP_(296, 2, "בשעת", "טרופכם")} "in the hour of your confusion"): the phrase\'s third seat glossed as at 250:2 and 275:2. Fresh.')
srow(296, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHEN YOU CAME OUT OF EGYPT" — IN THE HOUR OF YOUR REDEMPTION. ({SP_(296, 3, "בשעת", "גאלתכם")} "in the hour of your redemption"): find 2\'s three remembrances (23:5, 24:9, 25:17) glossed alike by the spine — one gloss for one phrase. Fresh.')
srow(296, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO MET YOU" (25:18) — "MET" MEANS ONLY "HAPPENED UPON YOU". ({SP_(296, 4, "אין", "קרך", "אלא", "שנזדמן", "לך")} "\'met you\' means only \'happened upon you\'"): the chance encounter — the root of 23:11\'s "chance of the night" (mikreh), a homograph of the camp\'s law in the war\'s enemy; 25:18 carries no head. Fresh.')
srow(296, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND CUT OFF THE STRAGGLERS BEHIND YOU" — HE KILLED ONLY THOSE DRAWN FROM THE OMNIPRESENT\'S WAYS, WHO FELL OUT FROM UNDER THE CLOUD\'S WINGS. ({SP_(296, 5, "שנמשכו", "מדרכי", "מקום")} "who were drawn from the ways of the Omnipresent"; {SP_(296, 5, "ונחשלו", "מתחת", "כנפי", "הענן")} "and fell out from under the cloud\'s wings"): the Mekhilta\'s reading of Exodus 17:8 (the English) — the tape\'s own attack retold; a REFERENCE ROW for the readback (the design). Fresh.')
srow(296, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND YOU WERE WEARY AND FAINT AND FEARED NOT GOD" — BY THE MEASURE YOU MEASURED THEY MEASURED TO YOU: AS YOU WERE WEARY AND FAINT AND FEARED NOT GOD, SO HE WAS WEARY AND FAINT AND FEARED NOT GOD. ({SP_(296, 6, "במדה", "שמדדת", "בה", "מדדו", "לך")} "by the measure you measured they measured to you"; {SP_(296, 6, "אף", "הוא", "עיף", "ויגע")} "he too was weary and faint"): MEASURE FOR MEASURE (Sotah 1:7\'s principle) — the verse\'s subject read both ways, Israel\'s and Amalek\'s (Onkelos gives it to Amalek, 25:18\'s row); "God" (Elohim) the chapter\'s one seat (find 14). Fresh.')
srow(296, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU REST FROM ALL YOUR ENEMIES AROUND" (25:19) — THAT NO BAND GATHER AGAINST YOU. ({SP_(296, 7, "שלא", "תאגד", "עליך", "אגדה")} "that no band gather against you"): THE CONDITION OF THE COMMAND — the rest from every enemy before Amalek\'s war: a STATE the command waits on (the design\'s DV25-05 — the king\'s war of 1 Samuel 15 the receipt ahead, the pointer OWED); 25:19 carries no head. Fresh.')
srow(296, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN THE LAND THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU FOR AN INHERITANCE TO POSSESS" — WHAT YOU WILL INHERIT YOU WILL CONQUER. ({SP_(296, 8, "מה", "שתירש", "תכבש")} "what you will inherit you will conquer"): the gift formula\'s seat (find 9 — 15:4 and 25:19 the only two "for an inheritance to possess it") — 180:1\'s and 297:1\'s trope (the English): the land\'s possession by war. Fresh.')
srow(296, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"BLOT OUT THE MEMORY OF AMALEK" — AND THERE HE SAYS (EXODUS 17:14) "I WILL SURELY BLOT OUT THE MEMORY OF AMALEK", AND (17:16) "A HAND ON THE THRONE OF THE LORD: WAR FOR THE LORD WITH AMALEK FROM GENERATION TO GENERATION". ({SP_(296, 9, "ולהלן", "הוא", "אומר")} "and there He says"; {SP_(296, 9, "מלחמה", "בעמלק", "מדר", "דר")} "war with Amalek from generation to generation"): THE TWO BLOTTINGS — the LORD\'s promise (Exodus 17:14, the tape\'s own line; find 10\'s run of five) and Israel\'s command, the same verb; the war "from generation to generation" the memory never wholly blotted (the English\'s note) — the chapter\'s, the portion\'s and the sitting\'s last row; 297:1 opens on 26:1 (the edge clean, the ink\'s assert). Fresh.')
